    <ferc:GeneralInformationAboutStatesInWhichRespondentServicesWereRendered id="f-341" contextRef="c-121">On February 26,1992, Yankee Atomic Electric Company permanently ceased power operations at the plant and commenced the process of decommissioning the Plant site.  To provide for interim storage of its spent nuclear fuel and greater-than-Class C ("GTCC") waste, the Company built an on-site independent spent fuel storage installation ("ISFSI") and completed the transfer of the Spent Fuel and GTCC to the new facility in April, 2003.</ferc:GeneralInformationAboutStatesInWhichRespondentServicesWereRendered>
